The endpoint issue is solver congruence over an opaque recursive function, not the program. I’m recasting the mathematical oracle as a tail-recursive Fibonacci fold `fibRun(a,b,i,n)`. That is extensionally Fibonacci from `(0,1,0,n)`, and it aligns one-for-one with each loop step, eliminating the unsupported congruence obligation.
apply patch
